# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database — from Supabase's "Connect" dialog, ORMs tab, Prisma
#
# Two strings that differ only by port. Supabase puts a traffic controller
# (a connection pooler) in front of Postgres, because serverless functions
# open far more connections than a database will tolerate.
#
#   6543 -> through the pooler. Normal app queries use this.
#   5432 -> straight to the database. Migrations need this, because changing
#           the database's shape needs one uninterrupted connection.
#
# Using the pooled URL for migrations makes them hang with no error.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATABASE_URL=""
DIRECT_URL=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Storage — from the same dialog, App Frameworks tab, Next.js
#
# One change from what that tab gives you: it offers the PUBLISHABLE key
# (sb_publishable_...), meant for browser code and deliberately weak.
# Uploads here happen on the server, so use the SECRET key instead
# (sb_secret_...), found under Settings > API Keys. It ignores every access
# rule in the project, so it must never be prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ and must
# never reach browser code.
#
# Supabase renamed these: anon -> publishable, service_role -> secret.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=""
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=""
SUPABASE_STORAGE_BUCKET="statements"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Extraction — console.anthropic.com
#
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL is optional and defaults to claude-sonnet-5. Set it to a
# cheaper model while iterating on prompt wording.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL="claude-sonnet-5"
